WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.654 --> 00:00:01.685
- Guys, here's the deal.

00:00:01.685 --> 00:00:03.387
Entrepreneurship, you're
going to have highs.

00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:05.621
You're going to have lows, I promise.

00:00:05.621 --> 00:00:07.428
But as long as you get yourself back up

00:00:07.428 --> 00:00:10.448
nothing can hold you back and stop you.

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:11.485
I was dead broke.

00:00:11.485 --> 00:00:12.866
In was bankrupt.

00:00:12.866 --> 00:00:14.161
In order to make ends meet,

00:00:14.161 --> 00:00:17.129
I was driving a beer
cart at a country club.

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:19.506
Success, it's up to you.

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:22.185
Don't let anybody dictate what is

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:23.589
going to make you feel fulfilled

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.344
and what makes you feel happy.

00:00:25.344 --> 00:00:27.087
I was pitching the Alpha M Style System.

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:28.087
- A to B to.

00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:32.637
- A solid idea, but at $300
a pop for a fashion formula?

00:00:32.637 --> 00:00:34.503
Customers just didn't bite.

00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:35.336
- Shocking.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:36.241
And neither did you.

00:00:36.241 --> 00:00:37.950
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.756
My one word is believe.

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:41.289
And I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:43.084
are going to solve all of the major

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:44.655
problems of the world.

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:45.828
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:45.828 --> 00:00:47.190
today we're going to learn from men's

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.387
lifestyle expert Aaron Marino.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:52.575
And my take on his top
10 rules for success.

00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:54.314
Rule number three is my personal favorite.

00:00:54.314 --> 00:00:56.590
And I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.099
And as always, guys as you're watching,

00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:00.002
if you hear something that really

00:01:00.002 --> 00:01:01.374
resonates with you, please leave it

00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:02.521
down in the comments below.

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:04.837
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:01:04.837 --> 00:01:07.215
And when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:01:07.215 --> 00:01:10.298
to stick for yourself as well, enjoy.

00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:16.555
(upbeat music)

00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:25.055
- My name's Aaron Marino.

00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:28.864
I am a men's lifestyle
expert and grooming guru.

00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:31.828
And if you would have told me 10 years ago

00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:33.752
that I would find so much happiness,

00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:37.431
joy, and fulfillment
making videos on YouTube,

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:39.291
I would have punched you in the face.

00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:41.732
My journey to finding this success,

00:01:41.732 --> 00:01:44.917
and happiness, and voice, unfortunately

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.426
wasn't a straight line.

00:01:46.426 --> 00:01:48.790
There were a lot of bumps
and turns along the way.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.509
And they ultimately started, a broke kid

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:54.837
from Philadelphia whose
parents got divorced.

00:01:54.837 --> 00:01:58.414
And I was raised with
an abusive stepfather.

00:01:58.414 --> 00:02:00.908
I lost my ability to stand up for myself.

00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:03.130
And so I kept everything inside.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.602
I had all this anger,
hostility, and resentment.

00:02:06.602 --> 00:02:10.957
My mom gave me a fitness
membership to a gym.

00:02:10.957 --> 00:02:14.522
And when I went, I found my home.

00:02:14.522 --> 00:02:18.223
It was the first time that
I felt like I belonged.

00:02:18.223 --> 00:02:20.993
From the age of 13, I knew exactly

00:02:20.993 --> 00:02:23.555
what I wanted to do with
the rest of my life.

00:02:23.555 --> 00:02:25.751
I was going to own a fitness center.

00:02:25.751 --> 00:02:28.113
I go to West Virginia
University, I graduate.

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:31.577
I met a guy, we opened
a few nutrition stores.

00:02:31.577 --> 00:02:33.837
And ultimately that didn't work out,

00:02:33.837 --> 00:02:36.838
because he was selling
drugs out of the back.

00:02:36.838 --> 00:02:40.248
And I realized that prison wasn't a place

00:02:40.248 --> 00:02:42.183
that I would flourish.

00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:45.187
And so I left there and I met a woman

00:02:45.187 --> 00:02:47.711
that I helped lose 100 pounds.

00:02:47.711 --> 00:02:49.024
And she came to me and she said,

00:02:49.024 --> 00:02:50.570
"Hey, I want to start a fitness center."

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.070
And this, for me was my dream.

00:02:54.287 --> 00:02:55.344
And it was tough.

00:02:55.344 --> 00:02:56.847
I didn't make much money.

00:02:56.847 --> 00:02:58.619
It didn't matter because I was happy.

00:02:58.619 --> 00:03:00.121
I was doing something that I loved.

00:03:00.121 --> 00:03:03.388
We took some loans and got some investors.

00:03:03.388 --> 00:03:05.872
There was a big issue
with one of our investors

00:03:05.872 --> 00:03:07.524
and my business partner.

00:03:07.524 --> 00:03:10.251
And it ultimately ended up in lots

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:12.086
of legal fights and battles.

00:03:12.086 --> 00:03:14.750
We had to end up shutting
down this business.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.348
I was dead broke.

00:03:16.348 --> 00:03:18.067
I was bankrupt.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.353
In order to make ends meet,

00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:22.627
I was driving a beer
cart at a country club.

00:03:22.627 --> 00:03:24.865
And I'm sitting there with tears

00:03:24.865 --> 00:03:27.972
rushing down my face because
I don't know where to go.

00:03:27.972 --> 00:03:31.820
I was at the lowest point
that I ever have been.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:33.808
Giving up was never an option.

00:03:33.808 --> 00:03:35.797
The problem was that I didn't know

00:03:35.797 --> 00:03:37.684
what success looked like anymore.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.101
But what I do have is a dream

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:43.574
and a desire to help people.

00:03:43.574 --> 00:03:45.211
At the time there really wasn't anything,

00:03:45.211 --> 00:03:48.108
any resources out there for regular guys

00:03:48.108 --> 00:03:49.954
to get some solid, basic advice

00:03:49.954 --> 00:03:52.154
on how to look good and feel great.

00:03:52.154 --> 00:03:55.663
I decided that I was going
to help men feel better

00:03:55.663 --> 00:03:57.641
and amazing about themselves.

00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:00.199
So, I have a video camera.

00:04:00.199 --> 00:04:02.770
I was the least tech savvy
person you'd ever meet.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.787
But I picked it up and I decided

00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:06.566
that I was going to try and film a video

00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:08.221
and put it on YouTube.

00:04:08.221 --> 00:04:10.119
Everything changed for me.

00:04:10.119 --> 00:04:11.432
I found that new vision.

00:04:11.432 --> 00:04:13.330
I found that new passion.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.980
All of a sudden I had a
voice, I had an audience.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.838
And I was doing something
that made me feel incredible.

00:04:19.838 --> 00:04:22.056
Because I realized I was doing something

00:04:22.056 --> 00:04:24.085
to help other people.

00:04:24.085 --> 00:04:26.450
And with YouTube I was able to help

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.421
millions of men around the world

00:04:29.421 --> 00:04:31.218
feel better about themselves.

00:04:31.218 --> 00:04:33.306
That's what I was put on this Earth to do.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.178
And I feel like true confidence

00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:37.830
comes from helping other people.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.596
All along I was searching for success.

00:04:40.596 --> 00:04:41.989
I thought success was going to mean

00:04:41.989 --> 00:04:44.850
a fitness center, a chain
of nutrition stores.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.009
And I put myself aside and just focused

00:04:47.009 --> 00:04:49.433
on the act of helping other people

00:04:49.433 --> 00:04:51.559
feel better about themselves.

00:04:51.559 --> 00:04:53.882
Everything in my life got better.

00:04:53.882 --> 00:04:56.100
At the core of it, it's
just helping others.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.823
Are you a risk taker?

00:04:57.823 --> 00:04:59.104
Successful people are, but not just

00:04:59.104 --> 00:05:01.583
random haphazard, like, "I'm driving

00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:03.740
"drunk without my seatbelt type of risk."

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.746
I'm talking about calculated risks.

00:05:05.746 --> 00:05:07.281
You weigh the options.

00:05:07.281 --> 00:05:09.599
You weigh the potential
outcome, both good and bad

00:05:09.599 --> 00:05:11.718
and you make the best decision possible.

00:05:11.718 --> 00:05:13.482
But guys, I'm here to tell you

00:05:13.482 --> 00:05:14.819
that you are never, ultimately

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:16.574
going to be successful unless you're

00:05:16.574 --> 00:05:18.098
willing to put yourself out there.

00:05:18.098 --> 00:05:19.680
Having the ability, or the willingness

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.664
to potentially fail,
is an absolute benefit.

00:05:22.664 --> 00:05:24.466
And sometimes, these calculated risks

00:05:24.466 --> 00:05:26.475
even though you thought about them,

00:05:26.475 --> 00:05:27.959
sometimes they just don't work out.

00:05:27.959 --> 00:05:31.251
And you know what successful people do?

00:05:31.251 --> 00:05:32.521
"That's all right, I learned something.

00:05:32.521 --> 00:05:34.103
"I know what not to do next time."

00:05:34.103 --> 00:05:36.338
And you make another calculated risk.

00:05:36.338 --> 00:05:38.426
Guys, nothing great was ever achieved

00:05:38.426 --> 00:05:40.585
because it was easy.

00:05:40.585 --> 00:05:42.369
So we talk all about the importance

00:05:42.369 --> 00:05:43.994
of knowing who you are.

00:05:43.994 --> 00:05:46.035
Having a secure sense of self is a key

00:05:46.035 --> 00:05:48.501
component to the confidence equation.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.461
"Who are you?

00:05:49.461 --> 00:05:50.778
"What are you capable of?"

00:05:50.778 --> 00:05:52.849
I've been asking myself this a lot lately.

00:05:52.849 --> 00:05:54.474
And it seems like the more I ask,

00:05:54.474 --> 00:05:56.910
the more I realize that over the course

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.464
of my life, I've been limiting myself

00:05:59.464 --> 00:06:02.174
due to some arbitrary set of restrictions

00:06:02.174 --> 00:06:05.394
or limitations that I've
put on myself years ago.

00:06:05.394 --> 00:06:07.061
And I know that I'm not alone.

00:06:07.061 --> 00:06:07.894
Why?

00:06:07.894 --> 00:06:09.134
This is the question that I need you

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:10.542
to start asking yourself.

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:12.368
Why do we have these limitations?

00:06:12.368 --> 00:06:14.805
What are our own personal limitations?

00:06:14.805 --> 00:06:18.646
Gentlemen, it is time to stop
living like the elephant.

00:06:18.646 --> 00:06:19.864
All right, now bear with me while

00:06:19.864 --> 00:06:21.808
I explain this elephant analogy.

00:06:21.808 --> 00:06:23.563
Okay, have you ever been to the circus?

00:06:23.563 --> 00:06:26.404
Have you ever seen those
big, massive elephants?

00:06:26.404 --> 00:06:28.044
They're held to the ground by this

00:06:28.044 --> 00:06:29.796
little rope and a tiny little stake.

00:06:29.796 --> 00:06:31.997
Are these elephants not strong enough?

00:06:31.997 --> 00:06:33.853
Is this, like, Kryptonite rope

00:06:33.853 --> 00:06:35.511
that these elephants are attached to?

00:06:35.511 --> 00:06:36.904
No, of course not.

00:06:36.904 --> 00:06:38.323
These elephants are bad ass.

00:06:38.323 --> 00:06:40.818
One tug of the tusk, they
could be out of there,

00:06:40.818 --> 00:06:42.022
and Delaware by dinner.

00:06:42.022 --> 00:06:43.962
But they don't, why?

00:06:43.962 --> 00:06:46.496
Because they've been
conditioned from a young age.

00:06:46.496 --> 00:06:48.746
When the little baby
elephants join the circus.

00:06:48.746 --> 00:06:50.894
I like to think of them as joining.

00:06:50.894 --> 00:06:53.805
(laughs)

00:06:53.805 --> 00:06:54.864
Poor elephants.

00:06:54.864 --> 00:06:56.201
Anyway, I digress.

00:06:56.201 --> 00:06:57.534
When these elephants are little,

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:58.867
they get to the circus and they

00:06:58.867 --> 00:07:00.536
put a big strong rope on them

00:07:00.536 --> 00:07:02.072
and they stake them to the ground.

00:07:02.072 --> 00:07:04.259
Now, at the time, these little elephants

00:07:04.259 --> 00:07:05.695
are like, "What the hell are you doing?"

00:07:05.695 --> 00:07:07.467
And they start jumping, and dancing,

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:09.264
and trying to get loose but they can't.

00:07:09.264 --> 00:07:10.670
Because they're little elephants.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:14.020
And this is a strong rope
and a big strong stake.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.817
So the elephant, after a while,

00:07:15.817 --> 00:07:18.805
gets it in his head,
"Hey, I can't get loose."

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:20.560
And so they stop trying.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:23.691
Because they know that
they can't get free.

00:07:23.691 --> 00:07:25.636
Well, the elephant grows up.

00:07:25.636 --> 00:07:27.155
The elephant gets to be a teenager.

00:07:27.155 --> 00:07:29.243
And he's getting stronger,
he's been working out.

00:07:29.243 --> 00:07:30.926
Then the elephant is an adult.

00:07:30.926 --> 00:07:33.030
By this time he is massive.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.187
He is strong.

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:36.391
He is capable of pulling out that stake

00:07:36.391 --> 00:07:39.394
and getting lost, but he doesn't.

00:07:39.394 --> 00:07:40.770
Because of his mindset.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.975
Because he remembers when he was little,

00:07:42.975 --> 00:07:45.656
he learned that he
couldn't and so he doesn't.

00:07:45.656 --> 00:07:47.138
And much like the elephant.

00:07:47.138 --> 00:07:49.065
The only thing holding us back.

00:07:49.065 --> 00:07:51.019
The only limitations that we have

00:07:51.019 --> 00:07:53.518
are these set of rules, or these things

00:07:53.518 --> 00:07:55.315
that we have created for ourself.

00:07:55.315 --> 00:07:58.518
These standards for ourselves
that we created years ago.

00:07:58.518 --> 00:08:00.841
A lot of time, it's
five, 10, 30 years ago.

00:08:00.841 --> 00:08:03.591
And just like the elephant,
we remained chained.

00:08:03.591 --> 00:08:05.769
It's time to analyze, identify,

00:08:05.769 --> 00:08:08.698
and give yourself the
permission to break the chains.

00:08:08.698 --> 00:08:11.586
Gentlemen, we are so incredibly powerful.

00:08:11.586 --> 00:08:13.614
The only thing that is holding you back,

00:08:13.614 --> 00:08:15.439
holding me back in our life, and from

00:08:15.439 --> 00:08:17.398
achieving whatever we want to achieve.

00:08:17.398 --> 00:08:20.063
Are these preconceived
notions that we can't.

00:08:20.063 --> 00:08:21.371
Was there somebody in your life that

00:08:21.371 --> 00:08:22.764
told you that you couldn't?

00:08:22.764 --> 00:08:24.519
That dissuaded you when, when you

00:08:24.519 --> 00:08:26.736
were a little kid, right?

00:08:26.736 --> 00:08:28.172
When you were a little kid what did

00:08:28.172 --> 00:08:29.304
you want to be when you grow up?

00:08:29.304 --> 00:08:30.667
An astronaut, everybody's
like, "A fireman.

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:32.624
"I want to be a police officer.

00:08:32.624 --> 00:08:34.707
"I want to be a ballerina."

00:08:36.059 --> 00:08:37.638
Whatever, don't look at me like that.

00:08:37.638 --> 00:08:39.556
It was possible at the time.

00:08:39.556 --> 00:08:41.464
But then what happens?

00:08:41.464 --> 00:08:43.670
Through your years, as you grow,

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.036
people are telling you, "No."

00:08:45.036 --> 00:08:46.631
People tell you, you can't.

00:08:46.631 --> 00:08:48.137
All right, it is incredibly rare

00:08:48.137 --> 00:08:49.989
to have and be surrounded by a nurturing

00:08:49.989 --> 00:08:52.342
environment where the people in your life

00:08:52.342 --> 00:08:54.747
tell you, "You can do
it, you can do anything.

00:08:54.747 --> 00:08:56.592
"You can achieve, you can strive.

00:08:56.592 --> 00:08:58.289
"You can go for the gold."

00:08:58.289 --> 00:09:00.536
But so often, all right, it's these

00:09:00.536 --> 00:09:02.291
negative people that stick out.

00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:03.524
"You can't do that.

00:09:03.524 --> 00:09:04.479
"You're not smart enough.

00:09:04.479 --> 00:09:05.652
"You're not fast enough.

00:09:05.652 --> 00:09:07.295
"You don't have the ability."

00:09:07.295 --> 00:09:10.759
And we hear this and in the
back of our head we adopt it.

00:09:10.759 --> 00:09:12.483
And we set these rules for ourselves,

00:09:12.483 --> 00:09:14.294
these self imposed limitations.

00:09:14.294 --> 00:09:16.718
Gentlemen, it's time to break the change.

00:09:16.718 --> 00:09:20.218
Change, change, (laughs).

00:09:21.168 --> 00:09:22.459
Do you have change for a dollar?

00:09:22.459 --> 00:09:23.995
Where do you have
limitations in your life?

00:09:23.995 --> 00:09:25.518
What is holding you back?

00:09:25.518 --> 00:09:27.446
You're absolutely strong enough,

00:09:27.446 --> 00:09:30.143
smart enough, fast
enough, confident enough.

00:09:30.143 --> 00:09:31.777
Gentlemen, it's time to start living

00:09:31.777 --> 00:09:33.536
with passion, with purpose.

00:09:33.536 --> 00:09:35.957
Okay, I realize that
are things in our life,

00:09:35.957 --> 00:09:38.207
we all have them, I have them.

00:09:38.207 --> 00:09:40.366
We all struggle with that
negative thought in our head.

00:09:40.366 --> 00:09:43.106
All right, these preconceived
notions, these limitations.

00:09:43.106 --> 00:09:44.558
Listen, I believe in you.

00:09:44.558 --> 00:09:46.964
You need to start believing in yourself.

00:09:46.964 --> 00:09:49.124
It absolutely kills me
and breaks my heart,

00:09:49.124 --> 00:09:51.532
whenever I see you guys and you're

00:09:51.532 --> 00:09:54.070
not living up to your potential
because of your limitations.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.254
And these limitations,
they're so arbitrary.

00:09:56.254 --> 00:09:58.796
There's absolutely nothing
to them, no foundation.

00:09:58.796 --> 00:10:00.972
Don't let other people set your

00:10:00.972 --> 00:10:02.840
expectations of yourself.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:05.013
Guys, you can do anything you want.

00:10:05.013 --> 00:10:09.019
Break the chains and stop
living like an elephant.

00:10:09.019 --> 00:10:10.933
One of the most eye opening pieces

00:10:10.933 --> 00:10:12.840
of advice that I've ever received

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.877
was when I heard that we teach

00:10:14.877 --> 00:10:16.774
people how to treat us.

00:10:16.774 --> 00:10:18.703
This idea was groundbreaking to me.

00:10:18.703 --> 00:10:20.588
And I started analyzing all of the

00:10:20.588 --> 00:10:22.470
different relationships that I had.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.167
And I realized that, absolutely,

00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:26.361
I was teaching people that it was

00:10:26.361 --> 00:10:28.955
okay to treat me a certain way.

00:10:28.955 --> 00:10:31.392
Because I would never stand up for myself.

00:10:31.392 --> 00:10:32.637
All right, there was a guy that I

00:10:32.637 --> 00:10:34.291
opened some nutrition stores with

00:10:34.291 --> 00:10:36.337
and I'd end up working more than I should

00:10:36.337 --> 00:10:38.121
because I could never say, "No."

00:10:38.121 --> 00:10:40.844
Or I want to make as
much money, make more.

00:10:40.844 --> 00:10:43.933
Or because I never would
stand up for myself

00:10:43.933 --> 00:10:46.760
and say, "No, I deserve it too."

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.226
Another reason that we as creatures

00:10:48.226 --> 00:10:50.444
have such a tough time standing

00:10:50.444 --> 00:10:51.644
up for ourselves is that we're

00:10:51.644 --> 00:10:54.245
afraid of what will
happen if we actually do.

00:10:54.245 --> 00:10:56.577
This was definitely the
case in my situation,

00:10:56.577 --> 00:10:57.969
when I was growing up.

00:10:57.969 --> 00:11:00.915
I was so petrified of having to move.

00:11:00.915 --> 00:11:04.539
Change schools, change
friends, that's what I loved.

00:11:04.539 --> 00:11:06.466
And it was easier for me just

00:11:06.466 --> 00:11:08.730
to take it at home, as opposed to

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.091
have to potentially move.

00:11:11.091 --> 00:11:12.817
And that's what the risk, I felt,

00:11:12.817 --> 00:11:14.660
was if I would stand up and say,

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.356
"Hey, that's not okay."

00:11:16.356 --> 00:11:18.010
Or if I would argue.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.516
So, in my early 20s, I
realized that I had a problem.

00:11:21.516 --> 00:11:23.692
My problem was the inability to

00:11:23.692 --> 00:11:25.649
basically stand up for myself.

00:11:25.649 --> 00:11:28.172
And it was really starting to bother me.

00:11:28.172 --> 00:11:30.262
And so I decided to go see a therapist.

00:11:30.262 --> 00:11:32.699
And it was one of the best
decisions I ever made.

00:11:32.699 --> 00:11:34.584
But unfortunately, one of the things

00:11:34.584 --> 00:11:37.614
I had to basically realize
and accept for myself,

00:11:37.614 --> 00:11:39.453
is that if I wasn't comfortable

00:11:39.453 --> 00:11:41.671
standing up for myself
in certain situations,

00:11:41.671 --> 00:11:43.443
with certain people, I needed to

00:11:43.443 --> 00:11:45.430
get out of those environments.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.357
Because it was never going to get better.

00:11:47.357 --> 00:11:49.853
The anxiety that I felt, even thinking

00:11:49.853 --> 00:11:52.896
about standing up for
myself was way too much.

00:11:52.896 --> 00:11:54.491
To me, it wasn't worth trying to

00:11:54.491 --> 00:11:56.898
work it out with this guy
that I was in business with.

00:11:56.898 --> 00:12:01.065
It was easier just to say,
"Deuces, I'm out," and leave.

00:12:01.963 --> 00:12:05.090
Because that's the choice I made.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:06.847
I don't know if it was right or wrong.

00:12:06.847 --> 00:12:08.585
I feel good about it.

00:12:08.585 --> 00:12:12.053
But a lot of times it is,
you've got to make a decision.

00:12:12.053 --> 00:12:13.808
Sometimes you're going to lose friends.

00:12:13.808 --> 00:12:15.736
Sometimes you're going to lose careers.

00:12:15.736 --> 00:12:17.924
You could potentially lose a significant

00:12:17.924 --> 00:12:21.214
other or spouse if you
finally stand up for yourself.

00:12:21.214 --> 00:12:24.262
But the alternative is you
being eaten alive inside.

00:12:24.262 --> 00:12:28.947
And that's just something I
wasn't willing to deal with.

00:12:28.947 --> 00:12:31.047
And when I left, I basically said,

00:12:31.047 --> 00:12:32.408
"Okay, if I'm going to be out of here

00:12:32.408 --> 00:12:34.468
"I need to change.

00:12:34.468 --> 00:12:35.920
"I need to make sure that I start

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.991
"asserting myself and
taking care of myself."

00:12:37.991 --> 00:12:40.122
And so, I started doing it.

00:12:40.122 --> 00:12:42.154
When I felt that I was
being treated poorly,

00:12:42.154 --> 00:12:43.618
I'd say something.

00:12:43.618 --> 00:12:45.227
Now one of the things that happened

00:12:45.227 --> 00:12:47.098
is I would get crazy butterflies.

00:12:47.098 --> 00:12:49.283
I would almost pass out.

00:12:49.283 --> 00:12:52.130
I would get so much
adrenaline and get so nervous.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:54.202
But it's like anything else.

00:12:54.202 --> 00:12:56.075
If you practice, the more you practice,

00:12:56.075 --> 00:12:57.683
the more you stand up for yourself.

00:12:57.683 --> 00:13:00.482
You're going to find, the
easier it's going to get.

00:13:00.482 --> 00:13:02.064
The other bonus and upside to standing

00:13:02.064 --> 00:13:04.077
up for yourself is that these toxic

00:13:04.077 --> 00:13:07.906
people and relationships,
seem to start going away.

00:13:07.906 --> 00:13:10.545
Because they're comfortable
putting you down.

00:13:10.545 --> 00:13:12.181
And if you're going to stand up they're

00:13:12.181 --> 00:13:13.562
going to be like, "I don't want, no I'll

00:13:13.562 --> 00:13:16.054
"go find somebody else who's a pushover."

00:13:16.054 --> 00:13:18.028
One of the things that we do.

00:13:18.028 --> 00:13:20.666
That totally prevents
us from moving forward

00:13:20.666 --> 00:13:22.884
and excelling in our lives, careers,

00:13:22.884 --> 00:13:25.510
relationships and
everything, is surrounding

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:27.467
ourselves with people that we really

00:13:27.467 --> 00:13:29.697
probably shouldn't be associating with.

00:13:29.697 --> 00:13:32.467
You are, all right, your success

00:13:32.467 --> 00:13:33.789
is going to be the average of

00:13:33.789 --> 00:13:35.106
the five people that you spend

00:13:35.106 --> 00:13:36.958
the most time with during the day.

00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:38.877
Now this is tough, all right.

00:13:38.877 --> 00:13:40.257
Because think about it, right now.

00:13:40.257 --> 00:13:42.736
Take an inventory of your
five closest friends.

00:13:42.736 --> 00:13:44.416
Or the five people during the day

00:13:44.416 --> 00:13:46.242
that you spend the most time with.

00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:47.795
Are they losers?

00:13:47.795 --> 00:13:49.984
Are you not exactly happy
with where you are right now?

00:13:49.984 --> 00:13:51.284
Well guess what?

00:13:51.284 --> 00:13:53.523
They're not going to
raise you up to the top.

00:13:53.523 --> 00:13:55.291
They're not going to make you look better.

00:13:55.291 --> 00:13:56.511
They're going to bring you down.

00:13:56.511 --> 00:13:57.945
Successful people surround themselves

00:13:57.945 --> 00:14:00.072
with successful people.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:02.352
Me personally, you know who
I want to be friends with?

00:14:02.352 --> 00:14:03.556
I want to be friends with people who

00:14:03.556 --> 00:14:06.914
are smarter, that are more successful.

00:14:06.914 --> 00:14:10.084
I want people that are
like, here, in my mind.

00:14:10.084 --> 00:14:12.213
I want to be here, I
want to be the low man

00:14:12.213 --> 00:14:13.274
on the totem pole.

00:14:13.274 --> 00:14:14.107
Why?

00:14:14.107 --> 00:14:15.345
Because I'm going to scurry up that

00:14:15.345 --> 00:14:18.581
freaking ladder like a
squirrel chasing a nut.

00:14:18.581 --> 00:14:21.363
All right, guys surround
yourself with successful people.

00:14:21.363 --> 00:14:23.337
If you're currently hanging out

00:14:23.337 --> 00:14:25.046
with people that don't have drive,

00:14:25.046 --> 00:14:27.120
don't have motivation,
that are kind of losers,

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:29.699
lovable losers, but losers nonetheless,

00:14:29.699 --> 00:14:32.848
re-evaluate your current
circle and adjust.

00:14:32.848 --> 00:14:34.818
If this means you've got to cut some ties

00:14:34.818 --> 00:14:37.528
or maybe not hang out
quite so much, it's okay.

00:14:37.528 --> 00:14:39.354
If you need to seek out other people

00:14:39.354 --> 00:14:41.488
to bring them into your
life, into your circle

00:14:41.488 --> 00:14:43.433
I suggest you do that as well.

00:14:43.433 --> 00:14:46.143
Success, as defined by Webster,

00:14:46.143 --> 00:14:49.548
"Is achieving wealth, respect, or fame."

00:14:49.548 --> 00:14:52.713
And I, personally, think
this definition sucks.

00:14:52.713 --> 00:14:54.884
And is exactly the reason why

00:14:54.884 --> 00:14:56.816
so many of us feel like failures,

00:14:56.816 --> 00:14:58.712
because we haven't lived up to

00:14:58.712 --> 00:15:01.264
some arbitrary set of success standards.

00:15:01.264 --> 00:15:03.120
And so today I thought we'd take a

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.382
little bit of time and talk about success.

00:15:05.382 --> 00:15:06.933
What it looks like to me.

00:15:06.933 --> 00:15:08.474
And what it looks like to you.

00:15:08.474 --> 00:15:10.773
Because, ultimately, you are the only one

00:15:10.773 --> 00:15:14.042
who can define what
success looks like to you.

00:15:14.042 --> 00:15:16.895
And I think it might
be time to re-evaluate.

00:15:16.895 --> 00:15:18.941
We are taught from a young age to win.

00:15:18.941 --> 00:15:21.549
All right, winning was success.

00:15:21.549 --> 00:15:22.653
It was the goal.

00:15:22.653 --> 00:15:24.757
Winning in sports, winning in your career,

00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:26.365
winning at life.

00:15:26.365 --> 00:15:30.249
The pursuit of life, liberty,
power, and a ton of money.

00:15:30.249 --> 00:15:32.686
This is what I thought that success

00:15:32.686 --> 00:15:34.266
was supposed to look like.

00:15:34.266 --> 00:15:36.890
Well every time I analyze myself

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:38.704
and my accomplishments, I ended up

00:15:38.704 --> 00:15:40.110
feeling like a failure.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.995
Because I didn't have power.

00:15:41.995 --> 00:15:43.910
I didn't have a lot of money.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:46.170
And I didn't have fame.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.589
And this is what I thought
it meant to be successful.

00:15:49.589 --> 00:15:51.696
Because in my mind that's what everything,

00:15:51.696 --> 00:15:53.986
everything in magazines, everything on TV.

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:56.208
If you were successful you got

00:15:56.208 --> 00:15:58.628
tons of cash and you got tons of power.

00:15:58.628 --> 00:16:00.976
Until one day I realized that I don't

00:16:00.976 --> 00:16:03.091
care about those things.

00:16:03.091 --> 00:16:04.774
All right, I don't want to be powerful.

00:16:04.774 --> 00:16:06.296
That's not my goal.

00:16:06.296 --> 00:16:08.038
I don't need tons of money.

00:16:08.038 --> 00:16:10.930
As long as I have enough to
be comfortable, I'm cool.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.403
Money wasn't my motivator.

00:16:12.403 --> 00:16:15.433
So why would I tie my
feelings of success to it.

00:16:15.433 --> 00:16:18.244
This realization rocked my world

00:16:18.244 --> 00:16:21.581
and totally changed my
perception of everything.

00:16:21.581 --> 00:16:24.524
And truly, it felt like a 1,000 pounds

00:16:24.524 --> 00:16:28.101
success weight was lifted
off of my shoulders.

00:16:28.101 --> 00:16:30.352
I felt amazing, I was free.

00:16:30.352 --> 00:16:31.758
So once I realized that this wasn't

00:16:31.758 --> 00:16:33.602
what success looked like, to me,

00:16:33.602 --> 00:16:35.051
now I got to figure it out.

00:16:35.051 --> 00:16:36.590
What does success look like?

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.256
What did I need to do?

00:16:38.256 --> 00:16:40.344
What did I need to accomplish in order

00:16:40.344 --> 00:16:42.549
to feel fulfilled and happy.

00:16:42.549 --> 00:16:44.073
And I figured it out.

00:16:44.073 --> 00:16:46.652
And this is what success looks like to me.

00:16:46.652 --> 00:16:49.582
My professional success meant that

00:16:49.582 --> 00:16:51.578
I was doing something that I loved.

00:16:51.578 --> 00:16:53.202
That I was able to touch other peoples'

00:16:53.202 --> 00:16:55.352
lives and make a difference.

00:16:55.352 --> 00:16:58.150
Personally, I was successful if have

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.558
relationships with
those people that I love

00:17:00.558 --> 00:17:02.544
that were deep and meaningful.

00:17:02.544 --> 00:17:04.586
Nothing was left off the table.

00:17:04.586 --> 00:17:06.197
You let people know how you feel.

00:17:06.197 --> 00:17:08.748
You communicate and reciprocate the love.

00:17:08.748 --> 00:17:10.301
Financial success, just meant that

00:17:10.301 --> 00:17:11.576
I had enough money.

00:17:11.576 --> 00:17:13.710
That I didn't need to worry about money.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.545
Not saying like, "Hey, I can go and buy

00:17:15.545 --> 00:17:17.029
"whatever I want because I don't really

00:17:17.029 --> 00:17:18.928
"have very expensive tastes."

00:17:18.928 --> 00:17:21.176
Meaning that, if I live modestly

00:17:21.176 --> 00:17:22.628
I don't have to worry about making

00:17:22.628 --> 00:17:24.496
it paycheck to paycheck.

00:17:24.496 --> 00:17:26.874
Emotional success to me meant that

00:17:26.874 --> 00:17:28.353
I was in touch with my feelings,

00:17:28.353 --> 00:17:30.005
my emotions, and that I was good

00:17:30.005 --> 00:17:31.369
with the person I saw looking

00:17:31.369 --> 00:17:33.061
back at me in the mirror.

00:17:33.061 --> 00:17:36.923
It was all about having a
solid character and confidence.

00:17:36.923 --> 00:17:38.560
If I can achieve those four things,

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:40.980
and not only achieve
them but maintain them,

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.518
let me tell you something.

00:17:42.518 --> 00:17:44.351
To me that is success.

00:17:45.346 --> 00:17:48.522
Every day when I wake up,
that is what I focus on.

00:17:48.522 --> 00:17:51.482
I focus on being successful
and what it means to me.

00:17:51.482 --> 00:17:53.944
It doesn't mean that I have a ton of cash.

00:17:53.944 --> 00:17:55.644
It doesn't mean that I have power,

00:17:55.644 --> 00:17:57.989
or fame, or worldly riches.

00:17:57.989 --> 00:18:00.905
No, but to some people that's
what success looks like,

00:18:00.905 --> 00:18:02.285
just not to me.

00:18:02.285 --> 00:18:04.124
So I wanted to share my story.

00:18:04.124 --> 00:18:05.661
To tell you, sort of, the journey

00:18:05.661 --> 00:18:07.664
that I took in order to identify

00:18:07.664 --> 00:18:10.185
and realize what success
actually meant to me.

00:18:10.185 --> 00:18:12.560
And I would encourage you to take

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:14.667
the time to figure it out for yourself.

00:18:14.667 --> 00:18:16.464
The first thing you need to do.

00:18:16.464 --> 00:18:18.059
And the first step is throwing out

00:18:18.059 --> 00:18:19.911
all those preconceived notions.

00:18:19.911 --> 00:18:21.292
All of the things you've been

00:18:21.292 --> 00:18:23.005
bombarded with from your parents,

00:18:23.005 --> 00:18:25.130
from society, from social media,

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:27.509
from TV, from movies, from everywhere.

00:18:27.509 --> 00:18:29.574
Throw it out, it doesn't matter.

00:18:29.574 --> 00:18:32.266
You get to start blank, clean slate.

00:18:32.266 --> 00:18:34.470
And figure out what
success looks like to you.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:36.750
Maybe success is you living on a beach.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.112
Being able to get up every morning

00:18:39.112 --> 00:18:40.791
and paint the ocean.

00:18:40.791 --> 00:18:41.997
I don't know, maybe success to you

00:18:41.997 --> 00:18:43.740
is having a family, having little kids

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.929
running home to you and just being a dad.

00:18:45.929 --> 00:18:47.929
Success, it's up to you.

00:18:48.786 --> 00:18:50.711
Don't let anybody dictate what is

00:18:50.711 --> 00:18:52.890
going to make you feel fulfilled

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:54.775
and what makes you feel happy.

00:18:54.775 --> 00:18:56.263
Guys, do it now.

00:18:56.263 --> 00:18:57.888
Figure it out, write it down.

00:18:57.888 --> 00:19:01.442
And then every single
morning you get up and focus.

00:19:01.442 --> 00:19:03.125
Focus on what it's going to take

00:19:03.125 --> 00:19:06.125
to make you feel whole
and feel successful.

00:19:06.125 --> 00:19:07.877
This, my friends, is a gift.

00:19:07.877 --> 00:19:10.255
And once you figure it out you are

00:19:10.255 --> 00:19:13.145
going to be amazed at how good it feels

00:19:13.145 --> 00:19:15.015
and how successful you become.

00:19:15.015 --> 00:19:17.319
The first place you need to start,

00:19:17.319 --> 00:19:20.915
when trying to become a
better man is attitude.

00:19:20.915 --> 00:19:24.034
It's all about changing your
mindset and perspective.

00:19:24.034 --> 00:19:25.469
All right, right now you're feeling

00:19:25.469 --> 00:19:26.513
a little bit crappy.

00:19:26.513 --> 00:19:27.514
You're like, "I'm not good enough.

00:19:27.514 --> 00:19:28.646
"I've got low self esteem."

00:19:28.646 --> 00:19:29.908
Here's the deal.

00:19:29.908 --> 00:19:32.110
You need to focus on all of the amazing,

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:34.938
positive, attributes that
you possess, all right?

00:19:34.938 --> 00:19:37.505
Change your mindset, you
will change your attitude.

00:19:37.505 --> 00:19:39.231
Because I tell you, you can have

00:19:39.231 --> 00:19:41.419
all the nicest clothes in the world,

00:19:41.419 --> 00:19:43.204
all the money, all the cars, everything.

00:19:43.204 --> 00:19:46.436
If you've got a crappy
attitude none of it matters.

00:19:46.436 --> 00:19:48.599
Your mindset, your
attitude, about yourself,

00:19:48.599 --> 00:19:51.367
about ourselves, that is
the hardest thing to change.

00:19:51.367 --> 00:19:53.166
But the thing, that once you get it,

00:19:53.166 --> 00:19:55.110
everything else seems to fall in place.

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:58.485
Confidence, this is what
Alpha M was all about.

00:19:58.485 --> 00:20:00.152
And what I would come to realize was

00:20:00.152 --> 00:20:03.111
the reason that I was put on this Earth.

00:20:03.111 --> 00:20:05.606
To help guys feel better about themselves.

00:20:05.606 --> 00:20:09.773
It's (laughs), it's hard
for me to talk about.

00:20:12.048 --> 00:20:14.367
This passion and this desire to help you

00:20:14.367 --> 00:20:16.784
burns so deeply inside of me.

00:20:17.807 --> 00:20:21.460
And I feel it through every
ounce of my body and soul.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.157
Confidence, this is the key to feeling

00:20:24.157 --> 00:20:25.593
great about yourself.

00:20:25.593 --> 00:20:28.058
Without it you will absolutely never know

00:20:28.058 --> 00:20:30.822
your true potential, or how amazingly

00:20:30.822 --> 00:20:33.177
powerful you could possibly be.

00:20:33.177 --> 00:20:35.252
So when I realized that
it was this confidence

00:20:35.252 --> 00:20:37.874
that I wanted to try and
facilitate in other people,

00:20:37.874 --> 00:20:39.959
I told some people about it.

00:20:39.959 --> 00:20:41.932
And they're like, "You
can't teach confidence.

00:20:41.932 --> 00:20:43.326
"Either you have it or you don't."

00:20:43.326 --> 00:20:46.152
And these were people that I did respect.

00:20:46.152 --> 00:20:48.606
And so it sort of got to me a little bit.

00:20:48.606 --> 00:20:50.342
And I thought to myself, "Hey, maybe you

00:20:50.342 --> 00:20:53.042
"can't teach or maybe you
can't learn confidence."

00:20:53.042 --> 00:20:54.927
They told me, "Just stick to style.

00:20:54.927 --> 00:20:58.319
"Don't talk about this other stuff."

00:20:58.319 --> 00:21:00.638
But I decided that I wanted to

00:21:00.638 --> 00:21:02.221
keep talking about the other stuff.

00:21:02.221 --> 00:21:04.397
Talk about things that I felt were

00:21:04.397 --> 00:21:06.324
important to develop character.

00:21:06.324 --> 00:21:09.603
Because I really did
feel like, "Hey, maybe

00:21:09.603 --> 00:21:11.849
"it's going to help at least one person."

00:21:11.849 --> 00:21:15.051
And then something remarkable happened.

00:21:15.051 --> 00:21:16.185
I got an email.

00:21:16.185 --> 00:21:17.832
It's from a guy who watched my videos.

00:21:17.832 --> 00:21:19.607
His name was Brian.

00:21:19.607 --> 00:21:22.447
And he told me that
through watching my videos,

00:21:22.447 --> 00:21:24.825
he actually felt better about himself

00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:27.333
and that he was more confident.

00:21:27.333 --> 00:21:29.278
And this was like, "What?"

00:21:29.278 --> 00:21:30.566
I'm like, "Really?"

00:21:30.566 --> 00:21:32.582
It was the best day of my life.

00:21:32.582 --> 00:21:35.250
And something else strange happened.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:36.685
I got another one.

00:21:36.685 --> 00:21:39.282
And another one, and another one.

00:21:39.282 --> 00:21:40.919
Gentlemen, I realized that I was right.

00:21:40.919 --> 00:21:43.865
You absolutely can learn to be confident.

00:21:43.865 --> 00:21:47.969
Validation, confidence is
a skill, it can be learned!

00:21:47.969 --> 00:21:49.286
But now came the tricky part.

00:21:49.286 --> 00:21:51.739
I needed to figure out a structure

00:21:51.739 --> 00:21:53.987
and a system how to actually walk

00:21:53.987 --> 00:21:56.921
somebody through the steps
to become more confident.

00:21:56.921 --> 00:22:00.018
It's taken me two years to
complete but I finally did it.

00:22:00.018 --> 00:22:01.874
Gentlemen, I am incredibly proud

00:22:01.874 --> 00:22:04.059
and pleased to announce, that the Alpha M

00:22:04.059 --> 00:22:06.195
Confidence Course is complete.

00:22:06.195 --> 00:22:07.964
The Alpha M Confidence Course is a

00:22:07.964 --> 00:22:09.730
step by step system to help you unlock

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:12.413
the five phases of self confidence.

00:22:12.413 --> 00:22:15.239
Phase one is learning and exploration.

00:22:15.239 --> 00:22:17.169
You've got to be able to
take a hard look at yourself.

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:19.260
Ask yourself the tough questions,

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:21.274
in order to drill down to figure out

00:22:21.274 --> 00:22:23.186
who you are as a person and what has

00:22:23.186 --> 00:22:25.640
led you to where you are now, as a person.

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:28.014
Until you understand who you are,

00:22:28.014 --> 00:22:29.655
you can never move forward.

00:22:29.655 --> 00:22:31.549
Phase two is developing your physical

00:22:31.549 --> 00:22:33.266
and external confidence.

00:22:33.266 --> 00:22:36.063
Fitness, style, grooming, diet.

00:22:36.063 --> 00:22:38.543
All of these topics are discussed,

00:22:38.543 --> 00:22:40.963
in detail, and outlined in phase two.

00:22:40.963 --> 00:22:43.880
Think of it as confidence
from the outside.

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:47.579
You work on the outside, it
transcends to the inside.

00:22:47.579 --> 00:22:49.200
And then Phase three is all about

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:51.927
acting and communicating confidently.

00:22:51.927 --> 00:22:54.364
Phase four is living confidently.

00:22:54.364 --> 00:22:56.070
And then we're wrapping
it up with Phase five

00:22:56.070 --> 00:22:57.592
which is adoption.

00:22:57.592 --> 00:22:59.759
But here's the interesting
thing about confidence.

00:22:59.759 --> 00:23:01.598
Any skill for that matter.

00:23:01.598 --> 00:23:03.845
Is that you need to
continually nurture it.

00:23:03.845 --> 00:23:05.150
And do the things that you did

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:08.725
in order to get to that
level of confidence.

00:23:08.725 --> 00:23:10.226
So if you get to be confident,

00:23:10.226 --> 00:23:11.707
feeling good about yourself, right?

00:23:11.707 --> 00:23:13.660
If you stop doing all those other things

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:15.781
that led you to here, guess what?

00:23:15.781 --> 00:23:17.578
The insecurity's going to creep in.

00:23:17.578 --> 00:23:19.111
Confidence is not a thing.

00:23:19.111 --> 00:23:20.625
It's not a destination.

00:23:20.625 --> 00:23:24.792
It's a journey that you're
going to be on your entire life.

00:23:26.695 --> 00:23:28.801
That's it guys, I got in trouble.

00:23:28.801 --> 00:23:30.600
After the gym I go home.

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:34.009
I eat, I shower, and I sit on the couch

00:23:34.009 --> 00:23:36.660
