00:27:18.092 --> 00:27:20.369
- True story, when I
had my fitness centers,

00:27:20.369 --> 00:27:22.209
it got pretty bad towards the end.

00:27:22.209 --> 00:27:23.576
I expanded too fast.

00:27:23.576 --> 00:27:25.775
There were a bunch of internal issues.

00:27:25.775 --> 00:27:28.026
Remember I was saying,
"Choose your partners wisely."

00:27:28.026 --> 00:27:30.840
It got so bad, financially, for us

00:27:30.840 --> 00:27:32.043
that I was having to take money

00:27:32.043 --> 00:27:34.347
off of credit cards in
order to pay my employees.

00:27:34.347 --> 00:27:36.841
And so, in order to make ends meet

00:27:36.841 --> 00:27:39.497
I had to take a second job on weekends,

00:27:39.497 --> 00:27:43.247
working as a beer cart
girl on a golf course.

00:27:44.311 --> 00:27:46.151
So, private, members only golf course.

00:27:46.151 --> 00:27:49.964
And there was a moment when, there were

00:27:49.964 --> 00:27:52.051
lots of moments doing
that, but it was Winter.

00:27:52.051 --> 00:27:53.692
It was February.

00:27:53.692 --> 00:27:55.039
And in Atlanta it does get cold,

00:27:55.039 --> 00:27:57.897
especially at 6:30 in
the morning, on a Sunday.

00:27:57.897 --> 00:27:59.130
There was frost.

00:27:59.130 --> 00:28:01.347
It was about 23 degrees and there was

00:28:01.347 --> 00:28:03.014
no heat in the cart.

00:28:03.869 --> 00:28:06.306
And so I'm sitting there waiting
for golfers to come around.

00:28:06.306 --> 00:28:08.553
There's no shelter, I'm just in this cart,

00:28:08.553 --> 00:28:10.289
shivering my butt off.

00:28:10.289 --> 00:28:13.136
And it was that critical moment,

00:28:13.136 --> 00:28:14.904
in my life, when I realized that,

00:28:14.904 --> 00:28:17.341
"My God, I will do anything it takes

00:28:17.341 --> 00:28:19.256
"in order to be successful."

00:28:19.256 --> 00:28:21.979
The walls, my empire that I had planned on

00:28:21.979 --> 00:28:24.617
building and creating was crumbling

00:28:24.617 --> 00:28:26.343
right before my eyes.

00:28:26.343 --> 00:28:28.169
And there I am sitting in a beer cart

00:28:28.169 --> 00:28:32.336
a 32 year old dude, serving
beer to drunk golfers.

00:28:33.215 --> 00:28:34.353
Swallow your pride.

00:28:34.353 --> 00:28:35.774
If you're going to do things, know that

00:28:35.774 --> 00:28:38.199
you're going to do it and
times could get tough.

00:28:38.199 --> 00:28:39.779
You give up too easily.

00:28:39.779 --> 00:28:42.968
When the tough gets going,
you do something else.

00:28:42.968 --> 00:28:44.472
Because the thought of actually

00:28:44.472 --> 00:28:46.910
having to persevere
and work through things

00:28:46.910 --> 00:28:48.941
is too much for you to handle.

00:28:48.941 --> 00:28:51.032
If you are somebody who gives up

00:28:51.032 --> 00:28:54.958
way too easy, you get any
slight hint of resistance

00:28:54.958 --> 00:28:56.943
in any capacity, you're like,

00:28:56.943 --> 00:28:58.671
"Whatever, I didn't want that anyway."

00:28:58.671 --> 00:29:00.004
And you're on to the next thing.

00:29:00.004 --> 00:29:01.747
If this is you, you are never going

00:29:01.747 --> 00:29:03.936
to ultimately achieve your goals

00:29:03.936 --> 00:29:06.937
and the desired success level
that you're striving for.

00:29:06.937 --> 00:29:08.880
Now I know that I personally have

00:29:08.880 --> 00:29:11.621
experienced quite a bit of
disappointment in my life.

00:29:11.621 --> 00:29:14.041
And I'm assuming that you have, as well.

00:29:14.041 --> 00:29:16.013
And guess what, we're going to continue

00:29:16.013 --> 00:29:18.346
to be disappointed throughout out lives.

00:29:18.346 --> 00:29:19.623
At least we should be.

00:29:19.623 --> 00:29:20.960
Because If you're not, that means

00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:22.715
that you're really not trying.

00:29:22.715 --> 00:29:25.164
Now how you handle yourself
post-disappointment,

00:29:25.164 --> 00:29:28.468
this is critical to your
emotional and mental well being.

00:29:28.468 --> 00:29:30.718
Pain, pain, hurting, right?

00:29:31.965 --> 00:29:33.632
It's part of the growing process.

00:29:33.632 --> 00:29:34.777
But I'll tell you something.

00:29:34.777 --> 00:29:37.155
Life has a funny way of closing doors

00:29:37.155 --> 00:29:39.591
in order to keep you moving
in the right direction.

00:29:39.591 --> 00:29:44.549
So often in our society and
as people we run from pain.

00:29:44.549 --> 00:29:46.881
We do everything we can
to protect ourselves

00:29:46.881 --> 00:29:49.621
and to shield ourselves
from feeling uncomfortable.

00:29:49.621 --> 00:29:50.959
That feeling of pain.

00:29:50.959 --> 00:29:52.394
And this is the reason why so many

00:29:52.394 --> 00:29:55.570
people abuse drugs, alcohol, casual sex.

00:29:55.570 --> 00:29:57.512
We do this to not feel the pain.

00:29:57.512 --> 00:29:59.065
But I'm saying, "Stop running.

00:29:59.065 --> 00:30:00.933
"Stop trying to mask it."

00:30:00.933 --> 00:30:04.271
When you feel pain,
disappointment, it's okay.

00:30:04.271 --> 00:30:05.735
Don't try and cover it up.

00:30:05.735 --> 00:30:07.937
What you should do is actually embrace it.

00:30:07.937 --> 00:30:10.241
I know, it's easy for me sitting here

00:30:10.241 --> 00:30:12.086
and saying, "Oh embrace the pain.

00:30:12.086 --> 00:30:13.361
"You're feeling like crap?

00:30:13.361 --> 00:30:14.451
"Don't worry about it.

00:30:14.451 --> 00:30:16.379
"Feel it, feel it."

00:30:16.379 --> 00:30:17.482
I get it, right?

00:30:17.482 --> 00:30:19.220
That's kind of a long shot.

00:30:19.220 --> 00:30:21.452
But what I'm saying is that the pain

00:30:21.452 --> 00:30:22.498
is normal, it's natural, it's a part

00:30:22.498 --> 00:30:23.887
of the growth process.

00:30:23.887 --> 00:30:26.206
Learn from it, once you do, you accept it,

00:30:26.206 --> 00:30:28.117
you embrace it, learn from it,

00:30:28.117 --> 00:30:29.560
and put it in its' place, you're going to

00:30:29.560 --> 00:30:32.384
be able to move forward,
stronger, faster, smarter.

00:30:32.384 --> 00:30:34.198
If you're not struggling and getting

00:30:34.198 --> 00:30:35.793
disappointed from time to time,

00:30:35.793 --> 00:30:37.359
this probably means that you're not

00:30:37.359 --> 00:30:39.493
really pushing your limits too far.

00:30:39.493 --> 00:30:41.971
All right, it's okay, embrace it,

00:30:41.971 --> 00:30:45.170
don't get discouraged, and stay focused.

